The trace isolated an unrelated ZooKeeper 3.4.4 SASL gating defect: after the readiness request wakes the selector, the client never enables socket writes because 3.4.4 incorrectly treats the default Java login configuration as an active SASL tunnel. I’ll validate the release’s built-in fallback path by naming a deliberately absent SASL login context; ZooKeeper catches that `LoginException`, disables SASL, and continues with the same unmodified NIO client transport. This does not constrain the socket or inject ZOOKEEPER-1560’s target condition.
